# GeT-RM reference material, Coriell ID NA19079 (Luhya in Webuye, Kenya,
# 1000 Genomes). GeT-RM consensus diplotype: *2/*5 (4/4 labs tested
# agreeing, including one confirmed by long-read single-molecule real-time
# sequencing). Source: Pratt VM et al., "Characterization of Reference
# Materials for TPMT and NUDT15: A GeT-RM Collaborative Project." J Mol
# Diagn 2022;24:1079-1088 (PMID 35850928), Table 2, as reproduced in CDC's
# public-domain data table
# (https://www.cdc.gov/lab-quality/media/pdfs/2024/08/TPMT-and-NUDT15-reference-materials_508C.pdf,
# retrieved 2026-08-19). Genotype below constructed from this project's own
# dbSNP-confirmed defining-variant coordinate (genes/nudt15.py), not
# redistributed from GeT-RM/Coriell/CDC directly.
#
# A genuinely valuable real-world case, not constructed to be interesting:
# per CPIC's Table 1, *2/*5 (one no-function allele + one decreased-
# function allele) is a real Poor Metabolizer. This module's one-locus
# scope only checks for the R139C substitution (which *2 carries, *5 does
# not) -- so *5 is entirely invisible to it. Presented with this genotype,
# this module correctly reports the R139C-heterozygous state it CAN see
# (*1/*3, Intermediate Metabolizer) but has no way to know a second,
# unmodeled no-function-adjacent allele (*5) is also present, so it
# undercalls severity relative to the true consensus diplotype. This is a
# real, documented limitation of the deliberate SNV-only v1 scope
# (genes/nudt15.py's module docstring), exposed here by real reference
# data rather than asserted abstractly -- the same discipline as DPYD's
# HG00118 case (docs/VALIDATION.md).
#CHROM	POS	ID	REF	ALT	QUAL	FILTER	INFO	FORMAT	SAMPLE1
chr13	48045719	rs116855232	C	T	99	PASS	.	GT	0/1
